winex11.drv: Use the desired state for mapping delays.

Backport of upstream Wine commit 2b05f63811f0e1acfd13e0f61d1a668b32a6de9a
(Rémi Bernon, 2026-06-30; Wine-Bug 59932), which the GE-Proton11-12 base
does not include. Upstream message:

  This matches the state the host window is supposed to be in, whereas
  pending_state is the state we have requested yet but which may need
  further requests.

Symptom it fixes here: a captioned window shown and hidden in one burst,
then given a second SetWindowPos(SWP_HIDEWINDOW) before the window
manager has answered the map, stays mapped while Windows reports it
hidden, as a blank window on screen. Shown by repro/p9-show-hide.

Adapted to the GE tree, whose layered-window check also tests
WS_EX_COMPOSITED. Drop this patch once the pinned base includes the
upstream commit.
Applies to: Valve Wine fda79a5 (GE-Proton11-12) after GE's preparation, in order after 0010.

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -3823,7 +3823,7 @@
            debugstr_window_rects(new_rects), new_style, swp_flags );
 
     /* visible windows are only hidden after SWP_HIDEWINDOW is used */
-    if (data->pending_state.wm_state != WithdrawnState && !(new_style & WS_VISIBLE) &&
+    if (data->desired_state.wm_state != WithdrawnState && !(new_style & WS_VISIBLE) &&
         !(swp_flags & SWP_HIDEWINDOW))
     {
         WARN( "win %p/%lx not yet hidden, delaying unmapping\n", hwnd, data->whole_window );
@@ -3831,7 +3831,7 @@
     }
 
     /* layered windows are mapped only once their attributes are set */
-    if (data->pending_state.wm_state == WithdrawnState && (new_style & WS_VISIBLE) &&
+    if (data->desired_state.wm_state == WithdrawnState && (new_style & WS_VISIBLE) &&
         (ex_style & (WS_EX_LAYERED | WS_EX_COMPOSITED)) == WS_EX_LAYERED && !data->layered && !IsRectEmpty( &new_rects->window ))
     {
         WARN( "win %p/%lx is layered, delaying mapping\n", hwnd, data->whole_window );
